    "title": "Farmington Municipal Schools to build Navajo hogan at middle school - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Fallon Fischer No media credit provided. ,\n10 hours ago\nFARMINGTON, N.M. (KRQE) – Farmington Municipal Schools is bringing tradition to life through building a Navajo hogan at Tibbetts Middle School. The purpose is to connect students with Diné culture, history, and community.\nWhat does an early bloom mean for Albuquerque plants and trees? The hogan will serve as a hands-on educational space where students will learn about Navajo traditions, values, and worldview. According to the University of New Mexico Libraries Tony Hillerman portal , a hogan is one of several traditional Navajo structures that have ceremonial significance.\nFarmington Municipal Schools said it is partnering with educators from Native American programs and experts to ensure the project is authentic, respectful, and educationally impactful.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRQE NEWS 13 - Breaking News, Albuquerque News, New Mexico News, Weather, and Videos.\n7",
    "summary": ", FARMINGTON, N.M. (KRQE) – Farmington Municipal Schools is bringing tradition to life through building a Navajo hogan at Tibbetts Middle School. The purpose is to connect students with Diné culture, history, and community. The hogan will serve as a hands-on educational space where students will learn about Navajo traditions, values, and worldview. According to the University of New Mexico Libraries Tony Hillerman portal , a hogan is one of several traditional Navajo structures that have ceremonial significance.",
